---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const drawings = (await getCollection('drawings')).sort((a, b) =>
  a.data.drawingId.localeCompare(b.data.drawingId)
);
const places = await getCollection('places');
const placeName = (id: string) => places.find((p) => p.id === id)?.data.name ?? id;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Drawings"
  description="Places from Larry Hunnewell's Vietnam service, 1964-1965, drawn from memory in his own hand."
>
  <span class="eyebrow">In his own hand</span>
  <h1>Drawings</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Sixty years on, Larry drew these places from memory in a sketchbook. They are not
    photographs and they are not maps: they are his memory, put on paper by him, with the
    names written the way he says them. Each drawing has a permanent archive number
    (<span class="record">VD-0001</span> onward), its own <strong>Memories</strong> box, and a
    place on the page of the place it shows, beside the photographs taken there.
  </p>
  <p class="record">
    {drawings.length} drawing{drawings.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} &middot; every legible inscription
    on a sheet is recorded, spelled as he wrote it &middot; nothing on a sheet is corrected
  </p>

  <ul class="drawing-grid">
    {drawings.map((drawing) => (
      <li>
        <a href={withBase(`/drawings/${drawing.id}/`)}>
          <img
            src={withBase(`/images/drawings/thumbs/${drawing.data.drawingId}.jpg`)}
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
            width="480"
            height="360"
          />
          <span class="record drawing-id">{drawing.data.drawingId}</span>
          <span class="drawing-title">{drawing.data.title}</span>
          <span class="record drawing-meta">
            {drawing.data.drawnDisplay}
            {drawing.data.depicts && <> &middot; {placeName(drawing.data.depicts.id)}</>}
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2>How to read them</h2>
  <p>
    A drawing from memory is evidence of what Larry remembers, which is what this archive is
    for. It is not evidence of where a building stood. Where a sheet agrees with what he has
    said at the photographs, the research notes say so; where it raises a question, the
    question is his to answer, and nothing on the sheet is checked against a map on these pages.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .drawing-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
  }

  .drawing-grid a {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    padding: 0.6rem;
  }

  .drawing-grid a:hover {
    border-color: var(--signal);
  }

  .drawing-grid img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .drawing-id {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .drawing-title {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .drawing-meta {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
